          "Pipeline parallelism partitions layer ranges but introduces stage imbalance, bubbles, and KV ownership. It is useful when model fit requires more devices and enough concurrent microbatches exist.",
          "That decision tree - replicate, then tensor-parallel within a node, then pipeline across nodes - is a dense-model tree. It assumes every device does the same work on every token, which a sparse mixture-of-experts model does not, and it assumes the binding constraint is either fit or collective latency, when for a sparse model it is memory capacity plus routing skew. Establish whether the model is dense or sparse before applying it.",
