    whyItMatters:
      "Retrieval quality is the part of enterprise RAG that gets tuned, and it is almost never the part that causes the incident. Incidents come from time: a group membership revoked at 09:14 that the vector index learns about at 09:40, a document deleted at the source and still resident in three derived stores, a citation that points at a revision the answer was not built from. Every chunk, embedding, posting-list entry, and cached answer is a copy that can outlive the authorization decision which permitted it, and each hop of an iterative retriever reopens that question from scratch. Get the versioning and revocation path right first; recall@k is the easier problem and the one that can still be fixed after launch.",
