          "Freeze the transform, not just the rows. A dataset manifest pins the conversation template, the tool schemas, which roles are loss-bearing, the stop tokens, and the truncation rule, and it hashes both the source record and its rendered form. Two runs that disagree about where the loss mask starts are two different experiments wearing one dataset name, and nothing in the loss curve will say so.",
          "Carry the provenance that decides whether an example may be used at all - the license or consent it arrived under, the annotator pool that produced it, its language and domain, and whether PII redaction has run - because that metadata is what makes a later takedown a query rather than an archaeology project. Split by source or task family so the same document cannot sit on both sides of the evaluation boundary.",
          "Gate the data before it reaches a GPU, and treat contamination as the expensive failure. Near-duplicate detection, invalid role ordering, answers leaked into prompts, and overlap with the benchmark you intend to report on are all cheap to test and unrecoverable once trained on: 2 percent benchmark overlap can buy several points on a public score that no user will ever experience, and it is only visible if someone checked before the run.",
